Xinerama: report the heads in screen order

ProcXineramaQueryScreens() walks the screens backward, so clients see the
last screen as head 0. Window managers put their taskbar on head 0 (IceWM's
XineramaPrimaryScreen), which then lands on the last monitor instead of the
first. Upstream X.Org reports screen 0 first; so does this.

diff --git a/Xext/panoramiX/panoramiX.c b/Xext/panoramiX/panoramiX.c
index 1a0f02e62..1723d4687 100644
--- a/Xext/panoramiX/panoramiX.c
+++ b/Xext/panoramiX/panoramiX.c
@@ -960,7 +960,8 @@ ProcXineramaQueryScreens(ClientPtr client)
     x_rpcbuf_t rpcbuf = { .swapped = client->swapped, .err_clear = TRUE };
 
     if (PanoramiXIsEnabled()) {
-        XINERAMA_FOR_EACH_SCREEN_BACKWARD({
+        /* in screen order: clients take the first head as the primary one */
+        XINERAMA_FOR_EACH_SCREEN_FORWARD({
             /* xXineramaScreenInfo is the same as xRectangle */
             x_rpcbuf_write_rect(&rpcbuf,
                                 walkScreen->x,
